  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<p>Correct answer: A</p>\n<p>A: The impulse is equal to the area under the force–time graph.<br/>- Impulse <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"= \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 0.40\\text{ s} \\times 40\\text{ N} = 8.0\\text{ N s}\"></span>.<br/>- From the impulse–momentum theorem, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"J = \\Delta p = m\\Delta v\"></span>.<br/>- <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"8.0\\text{ N s} = 2.0\\text{ kg} \\times (v - 0) \\implies v = 4.0\\text{ m s}^{-1}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>B: This value arises if the factor of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{2}\"></span> is omitted when calculating the triangular area (Impulse <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"= 16\\text{ N s}\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v = 16 / 2 = 8\"></span>).</p>\n<p>C: This value arises if the area is calculated as <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.40 \\times 40\"></span> and the mass of the object is ignored.</p>\n<p>D: This value arises if the student simply divides the peak force by the mass (<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{40}{2.0}\"></span>), ignoring the time variation.</p>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_1a",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A net force <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span> acts on an object of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.0\\text{ kg}\"></span> which is initially at rest. The variation with time <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t\"></span> of the force <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span> is shown in the graph.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>What is the speed of the object at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = 0.40\\text{ s}\"></span>?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4.0\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"8.0\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"16\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"20\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
